From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Brooks <bass_rock@me.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(amdgpu): keep GTT cached and snooped, as Stela's build
 leaves every page's kernel mapping write-back

TTM's pool makes a write-combined page's kernel mapping write-combined
(set_pages_array_wc) only under CONFIG_X86, which Stela's build does not
set. A USWC BO's client mapping then aliases a write-back kernel mapping
holding the lines the page's zeroing left in the CPU's caches, while the
GPU reads and writes the page unsnooped. Offer no USWC, as amdgpu does
where write-combining cannot work.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
index 718937777e5323723a96f33492cf7e3594914269..483c6fa5bb23a2a7bb688e73900f406a02d0eee7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
@@ -582,6 +582,17 @@ static bool amdgpu_bo_validate_size(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
 
 bool amdgpu_bo_support_uswc(u64 bo_flags)
 {
+	/* Stela: TTM's pool makes a write-combined page's kernel mapping
+	 * write-combined too (set_pages_array_wc) only under CONFIG_X86, which
+	 * Stela's build does not set: every page keeps its write-back kernel
+	 * mapping, with the lines its zeroing left in the CPU's caches. A
+	 * write-combined client mapping of such a page aliases that mapping,
+	 * and the GPU reads and writes the page unsnooped, so neither the
+	 * CPU's view nor the GPU's is the page's. Keep GTT cached and snooped,
+	 * as a kernel that cannot change a page's caching does. */
+	if (bo_flags & AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_CPU_GTT_USWC)
+		DRM_INFO_ONCE("Stela: GTT stays cached and snooped; USWC is not offered\n");
+	return false;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_X86_32
 	/* XXX: Write-combined CPU mappings of GTT seem broken on 32-bit
